From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 01:57:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08038/11362] The induce path accepts broken code 13 times in
 15; a second ask of ANY kind is what rescues it

PHASE 2 asked for the funnel effect: how many of the five audited games now produce a usable
engine that faces the semantic gate. Measured live, three arms, 5 games x 3 attempts on
gemma-4-31B-it Q4_K_M -- CUDA build proven from /proc/<pid>/exe, 21416 MiB per-PID VRAM on
each of two 3090s, n_ctx=32768, non-default ports, prompts captured LLM-OFF from the agent
itself and byte-identical to Phase 1's committed ft09 prompt (sha 78f829d86fa65938).

  arm                                        usable      games with a non-degenerate engine
  A shipped (round 0 only)                   1 / 15      tn36
  B repair (names the defect + exception)    3 / 13      sc25, tn36
  C control (neutral re-ask, names nothing)  2 / 13      ft09

Games reaching in_sample_cell_recall > 0.5: 1 of 5 -> 3 of 5. tu93 and lp85 get nothing good
from any arm.

THE FINDING THAT IS NOT CLOSE: the shipped generate() ACCEPTED a candidate carrying a
mechanical defect in 13 of 15 attempts. It never re-asks because it does not know anything is
wrong. That is the mechanism the static check adds, and it is the part worth having.

THE ONE THAT IS CLOSE, AND I OVER-READ IT FIRST. Repair 3 vs control 2 reads as a repair win,
and the first version of build_ab_artifact.py printed exactly that -- "the DEFECT TEXT carries
the value". The comparison is PAIRED (both arms branch from the same round 0 at the same seed
and temperature), so only discordant pairs inform it: 5 discordant, 3 repair-only, 2
control-only, exact two-sided sign test p = 1.000. A coin. The arms also succeed on DISJOINT
games, which is itself the signature of resampling rather than comprehension. The over-claim
was in the MEASUREMENT TOOLING rather than in a result -- the worse place, because a result
gets audited and a verdict string gets quoted. The tool now computes the paired test, and
SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-6052-7 requires the control arm for any future repair claim.

"USABLE" IS NECESSARY AND NOWHERE NEAR SUFFICIENT. Scored with the production
WorldModelVerifier, tu93's one usable repair has cell_recall 0.112, change_fidelity 0.076, 144
INVENTED cells and 0 of 25 real changes right -- it clears the non-inert clause by changing the
grid WRONGLY. Two of the five usable engines are degenerate. SCENARIO-8 now requires the
verifier's own numbers beside any usable count.

THREE INDEPENDENT REPRODUCTIONS OF THE 2026-07-30 AUDIT, from the generator side. ft09's best
completion scores cell_recall 0.947 / noop_hallucination 0/19 against the audit's 0.947 -- the
same mechanic, rediscovered. tn36's round 0 scores 1.000/1.000/1.000 at 25/25, the audit's
"run's best engine". lp85's best repair scores accuracy 0.920 with cell_recall 0.000 and 0/2
changes right -- the vacuous pass the audit flagged, matching 23 of 25 transitions by matching
the 23 no-ops; `usable` rejects it and a 0.5 legacy-accuracy bar would admit it. All in-sample,
labelled as such: the live gate grades a held-out suffix the capture does not preserve.

A REAL LATENT BUG IN MY OWN MODULE, found by self-review after the first commit.
_find_function used a bare ast.walk with "last definition wins". ast.walk is BREADTH-FIRST, so
every module-level definition is visited before any nested one -- the rule reliably picked the
NESTED engine whenever one existed, while exec binds only top-level ones. A helper's throwaway
inner function would have decided the verdict for the real engine, in either direction. Fixed,
two tests, mutation-proven. Inert on the corpus: no generated engine defines a nested engine
and the 439-file scan is byte-identical either way -- a latent bug, not an active one.

Also capped the code echoed into a repair prompt. The completions being repaired are
repetition-loop runaways; echoing one back in full spends thousands of prompt tokens
re-showing the model the text it is stuck repeating.

NOT WIRED IN, deliberately. The validator is standalone and nothing in the shipped induce path
calls it. Editing arc_executable_world_model.py marks 7 registered artifacts stale, and the
honest justification for paying that is a proven funnel gain. What is proven is a diagnosis
(13 of 15) and an UNDECIDED repair mechanism (p = 1.000). Wiring a re-ask into the SCORED path
on that evidence would be a behaviour change ahead of its warrant -- the same call Phase 1 made
about repeat_penalty, for the same reason. The cheap next measurement this points at is arm A
versus a plain re-ask with NO defect text, at larger n.

46 tests, 14/14 mutations killed. REQ-ARC-WMTE-6052 + SCENARIO-7/-8. Banked ARC levels remain
3/3 and the submission gate is NOT met.

